{"name":"Conte Crayon","hex":"#bb4745","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"conte","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An Italian count."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conte"},{"term":"crayon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A stick of colored chalk or wax used for drawing.","A colored pencil, a colouring pencil"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To draw with a crayon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crayon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Conté","blocks":[{"text":"Conté, also called the Conté stick or Conté crayon, is a drawing medium composed of compressed powdered graphite or charcoal mixed with a clay base, square in cross-section. It was invented in 1795 by Nicolas-Jacques Conté, who created the combination of clay and graphite in response to the shortage of graphite caused by the Napoleonic Wars. Conté crayons had the advantage of being cost-effective to produce, and easy to manufacture in controlled grades of hardness."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Cont%C3%A9_crayons.JPG/330px-Cont%C3%A9_crayons.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cont%C3%A9","wikidata":"Q1129270"},{"title":"Crayon","blocks":[{"text":"A crayon is a stick of pigmented wax used for writing or drawing. Wax crayons differ from pastels, in which the pigment is mixed with a dry binder such as gum arabic, and from oil pastels, where the binder is a mixture of wax and oil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Crayones_cera.jpg/330px-Crayones_cera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crayon","wikidata":"Q69158"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Kurasaw-rashomon.jpg/500px-Kurasaw-rashomon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":